ember poll showed a statistical tie and several raters call the race a Tossup, so the margin stays narrow. Markets price Wagner around 70% to win, consistent with a Lean R outlook.", "watch": "Any additional independent polling or outside spending in the St. Louis suburbs could confirm a genuine tie or restore Wagner's cushion.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Ann Wagner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ann Wagner seeks another term in a St. Louis-area seat that leans Republican by about four points. She has raised $3.5 million and holds a large cash advantage over Democrat Fred Wellman, a former Army officer who won his primary in August. Outside groups have spent modestly against her, and she has publicized federal funding wins for the district.\n\nThe race looks closer than the district's lean suggests. A mid-September poll showed Wagner up only one point, within the margin of error, and ratings are split: several outlets call it Likely R, while others rate it Lean R or even Tossup. Prediction markets give Wagner roughly a 70% chance. The fundamentals point to a narrow but real Republican edge, with Wellman needing a strong closing argument on ethics and incumbency fatigue to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2379, "margin": -4.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2517, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2065, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.22, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1903, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2785, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3439, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3337, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3474, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3548, "margin": -2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.378, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05